title: 'pallet-scarcity: coinage-style NFT ownership with feeless rest-time-prioritized transfers'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Adds `pallet-scarcity`, a FRAME pallet for collectible instances under a
    coinage-style ownership model: one instance per fresh purse public key,
    with a stable `InstanceId` reverse index as the external handle. Item
    identity is immutable once written and may be minted many times. Metadata
    is a two-level mutable key/value store: collection entries provide
    defaults and item entries override the same key. Only the collection owner
    may write either scope; each entry has its own deposit and there is no
    metadata freeze mechanism.

    Storage deposits are paid on the supply side: the creator pays for a
    collection, the issuer pays for each item definition, and the collection
    owner pays for each metadata entry and ordinarily minted instance. Trusted
    claim-path mints waive only the instance deposit because their volume is
    bounded by claim credits.

    Transfers and burns are feeless and authorized by the owning purse key
    through the `AsScarcity` transaction extension, which elevates a custom
    `Origin::Nft` capability origin, consumes the instance in `prepare`,
    assigns transaction priority proportional to the instance's rest time
    (seconds since it last moved, capped), and restores the instance with a
    quadratic backoff lock when dispatch fails. Burning releases any instance
    deposit while keeping item supply monotonic. The separate replay-epoch
    field was removed as unnecessary: the replay model is nonce-free through
    consumption-on-use, a per-key `provides` tag, transaction mortality, and
    failure locks.

    A `try_state` hook verifies the owner/reverse-index bijection and rejects
    orphaned instance-deposit tickets and metadata. Metadata growth is priced
    by a deposit per entry; `define_item` accepts a linearly weighted `Vec`
    whose batch size is bounded by extrinsic and block length, while each key
    and value remains individually bounded.
crates:
- name: pallet-scarcity
  bump: major
- name: polkadot-sdk
  bump: minor
